                <comment text="// Here we add focus listeners to the component. The funny code is because we need"/>
                <comment text="// to guarantee that the AutoCompleteListener - if used - is called before fieldListener"/>
                <comment text="// on a focus lost event. The AutoCompleteListener is responsible for removing any"/>
                <comment text="// current suggestion when focus is lost, and this must be done before fieldListener"/>
                <comment text="// stores the current edit. Swing doesn't guarantee the order of execution of event"/>
                <comment text="// listeners, so we handle this by only adding the AutoCompleteListener and telling"/>
                <comment text="// it to call fieldListener afterwards. If no AutoCompleteListener is used, we"/>
                <comment text="// add the fieldListener normally."/>
